-- title:
--   Finitely generated homogeneous ideal cutting out a closed subscheme of Pⁿ_A
-- statement:
--   Let $A$ be a commutative ring, let $n$ be a natural number, let $Z$ be a scheme, and let $\iota : Z \to \operatorname{Proj}\bigl(\bigoplus_d A[x_0,\dots,x_n]_d\bigr) = \mathbb{P}^n_A$ be a morphism, where the graded ring is the homogeneous submodule grading of `MvPolynomial (Fin (n+1)) A`. Assume $\iota$ is a closed immersion and that the composite of $\iota$ with the structure morphism `ProjSpace.π A n :` $\mathbb{P}^n_A \to \operatorname{Spec} A$ is locally of finite presentation. Then there exists an ideal $I_0 \subseteq A[x_0,\dots,x_n]$ such that: $I_0$ is finitely generated; $I_0$ is homogeneous in the sense that every homogeneous component `homogeneousComponent d p` of every $p \in I_0$ again lies in $I_0$; and for every index $i \in \{0,\dots,n\}$ the ideal attached by the kernel ideal sheaf data `ι.ker` to the affine open $D_+(x_i)$ (affine by `Proj.isAffineOpen_basicOpen`, $x_i$ being homogeneous of degree one) is the ideal generated by the set of sections of the form $\mathrm{image\ under\ }$ `Proj.awayToSection` of the degree-zero homogeneous localisation $F/x_i^{\,d}$, as $d$ runs over natural numbers and $F$ over elements of $I_0$ homogeneous of degree $d$. Thus on each standard chart the ideal of $Z$ is generated by the dehomogenisations of the forms in $I_0$.
--
--   This is the standard statement that a closed subscheme of projective $n$-space over a ring which is locally of finite presentation over the base is cut out, chart by chart, by the dehomogenisations of finitely many forms, the finitely generated homogeneous ideal $I_0$ replacing the full (possibly non-finitely-generated) saturated ideal of $Z$. It is used in the construction of the scheme representing the functor of flat, locally finitely presented closed subschemes of $\mathbb{P}^n$ with prescribed Hilbert polynomial.
